# L1 corrections (Addendum A1). Batch files stay as checkpointed; compiled by _tools/corrections.py into CORRECTIONS.jsonl.

# --- END-OF-RUN-CONSISTENCY: reading differences listed during the run and reconciled at its end.
@ COR-L1-0001 FG-L1-14607d9618 END-OF-RUN-CONSISTENCY | The record's claim includes the servicing clause, which DEP-008 does not state; a stronger claim is never CANONICAL_ONLY (C1). Same reading as FG-M-f830eb5293 and FG-M1-ee2a76fc04.
  set code: CD
  set k: P
  set c: M
  set x: on the latest stable servicing release
  set s: A project stays on an older .NET 10 servicing release: DEP-008 is satisfied; L1's statement is not.
  set note: Restates DEP-008; the servicing release is the remainder.
  recheck: Re-read the record's evidence and DEP-008's text.
@ COR-L1-0002 FG-L1-21ae6647aa END-OF-RUN-CONSISTENCY | ARC-008 names transport types, while the check rejects the framework and packages in Application whatever they are used for. C3 keeps CANONICAL_ONLY only for an identical rule. Same reading as FG-K1-35ac3364ed.
  set code: CD
  set m: MN
  set st: S
  set k: W
  set c: M
  set x: any Microsoft.AspNetCore.* package, a web SDK or the shared framework in Application is an error, even with no transport use
  set s: Application references Microsoft.AspNetCore.Cryptography.KeyDerivation and uses no transport type: ARC-008 is satisfied; L1's check reports an error.
  set note: ARC-002 covers Domain. ARC-008 names transport types; the check is broader in Application.
  recheck: Re-read check-architecture.mjs:90-106 and ARC-008's text.
@ COR-L1-0003 FG-L1-591aa8deca END-OF-RUN-CONSISTENCY | Same check as FG-L1-21ae6647aa.
  set code: CD
  set m: MN
  set st: S
  set k: W
  set x: the ASP.NET Core shared framework in Application is an error, even with no transport use
  set s: As for FG-L1-21ae6647aa.
  set note: Same check. Name-pattern mapping is how the check finds roles and adds no duty.
  recheck: Re-read check.json:6-17.
@ COR-L1-0004 FG-L1-f0cf2d0f61 END-OF-RUN-CONSISTENCY | Same check as FG-L1-21ae6647aa; the prefix match is what reaches beyond transport types.
  set code: CD
  set m: MN
  set st: S
  set k: W
  set x: inner-role checks reject direct framework references, implying SDKs and package-name prefixes, including neutral APIs
  set s: As for FG-L1-21ae6647aa.
  set note: Same check, as reported: the overmatch of neutral APIs is the remainder.
  recheck: Re-read check-architecture.mjs:90-110.

